    description: "Go structural interface satisfaction now checks (name, param_count, return_count) tuples instead of just method names. This prevents false implements edges when methods share names but have different signatures (e.g., Close() error vs Close(ctx) error). Validated by unit tests; needs bakeoff confirmation that alertmanager dispatches_to edge count drops significantly from the previous 463."  # 2a28
    fields:  # 2a28
      statement: "Go structural interface matching verifies method arity (param_count, return_count) alongside names, preventing false implements edges from coincidental name collisions"  # 2a28
      root_cause: "_extract_interface_methods and struct_method_sets used set[str] of method names only; Go requires matching full signatures for interface satisfaction"  # 2a28
